  partName: High Pressure Turbine Shaft
  description: The Right Inner Cover is a large, elongated component situated at
    the middle-right-center of the engine, made from Inside cover1 material. It serves
    as a protective casing for the engine's internal components, shielding them from
    external damage and debris. Interestingly, its elongated shape allows for a snug
    fit around the engine's core, providing comprehensive coverage and support.
